#. Source: input/pagecontent/business-processes.md:367
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/business-processes.html
#: input/pagecontent/business-processes.md:367
msgid "Audit. Once an agreement applies, {code0} records an IHE ATNA audit event ({code1} Record Audit Event). It cites the fixed-version URL of every agreement and Consent evaluated, which of them permitted, the combining DMN decision used (by namespace, decision id, and its file's fixed-version URL and SHA-256), the receiver, the purpose of use, and the documents released (or the refusal). This follows the VHL profile's own ATNA grouping: Vol 1 §1:XX.3 requires the VHL Sharer and the VHL Receiver to be grouped with an ATNA Secure Node or Secure Application for {code2}, and §1:XX.6.1 gives that grouping its audit logging. VHL itself says the Sharer SHOULD log access (ITI-YY5 §2:3.YY5.5.6) and MAY record the Audit Event – Accessed Health Data (ITI-YY5 §2:3.YY5.4.1.7). Under an agreement, the event is always recorded. IHE BALP needs owner approval (Trial Implementation). The PROV-O record of process G ({code3}) cites the same agreement URLs and DMN decision, so the ATNA log and the PROV log agree."
msgstr ""

#. Source: input/pagecontent/business-processes.md:224
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/business-processes.html
#: input/pagecontent/business-processes.md:224
msgid "Audit. The ATNA event ({code0}, {code1}) and the PROV-O record ({code2}) cite every agreement and Consent evaluated, and which of them permitted."
msgstr ""

#. Source: input/pagecontent/business-processes.md:289
#. URL: http://smart.who.int/trust-phw/business-processes.html
#: input/pagecontent/business-processes.md:289
msgid "Audit. The ATNA event cites the agreement's fixed-version URL, the requester, the purpose of use, the data or documents released, and the decision. ATNA is reached in the same way the VHL profile reaches it. VHL Volume 1 §1:XX.3, Table XX.3-1, requires the VHL Sharer and VHL Receiver to be grouped with an ATNA Secure Node or Secure Application. §1:XX.6.1 covers the secure channel ({code0}) and audit logging. Those sections are from the IHE/ITI.VHL source at commit {code1}, as snapshotted in litlfred/smart-trust-tools {code2}. IHE BALP (Basic Audit Log Patterns) is Trial Implementation and needs owner approval before this IG names its AuditEvent patterns. The PROV-O record ({code3}) cites the same agreement URL, so the two logs agree."
msgstr ""

